WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
Look inside a gold atom.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.320
Its nucleus is roughly 20 000
times smaller than the whole atom.

3
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:11.670
Yet that tiny nucleus holds
nearly all the atom's mass.

4
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.280
Now imagine squeezing out the empty space,

5
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.850
and filling a teaspoon with
nothing but nuclear matter.

6
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.690
How heavy would that one teaspoon be?

7
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.950
In this mission, you'll find the rule
linking a nucleus's radius to the number

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.910
of nucleons inside it.

9
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.060
Then you'll calculate the
radius of a gold-197 nucleus,

10
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.650
from that rule.

11
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.330
Your mission: calculate the mass of
a teaspoon of pure nuclear matter.
